From 1919d8d4388961e369ae23d84b28013bdc953fcf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 17:52:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ether: override Google (MindTheGapps) SetupWizard so
 Lineage's handles first boot

Add MindTheGapps' SetupWizard + GooglePartnerSetup to LineageSetupWizard's
overrides (the mechanism MindTheGapps itself uses to drop Provision). On GApps
builds com.google.android.setupwizard otherwise takes precedence and taps land
offset on the welcome screen, so setup can't be completed; dropping it restores
the Lineage wizard (still handles Google sign-in). No-op on non-GApps builds.

The module names matter and differ by branch. MindTheGapps called these
SetupWizardPrebuilt and PartnerSetupPrebuilt on lineage-18.1; on 20.0 they are
plain SetupWizard and GooglePartnerSetup (vendor/gapps arm64/Android.bp and
common/Android.bp). Soong's overrides match by module name and say nothing when a
name does not exist, so the 18.1 names here built cleanly and shipped Google's
wizard anyway -- which is what happened, and is only visible on the phone at first
boot.
---
 Android.bp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Android.bp b/Android.bp
index a577115..7767905 100644
--- a/Android.bp
+++ b/Android.bp
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@ android_app {
     system_ext_specific: true,
     platform_apis: true,
 
-    overrides: ["Provision"],
+    overrides: ["Provision", "SetupWizard", "GooglePartnerSetup"],
 
     optimize: {
         proguard_flags_files: ["proguard.flags"],
-- 
